## Authentication
Bearer Token — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `POST /api/v1/auth/token` — Obtain an authentication token for API access.
- `POST /v1/sourceToken` — Obtain a source token for authentication.

### Data Read (3)
- `GET /api/surveys/` — Retrieve survey data.
- `GET /api/v1/ghost/{ghostHash}` — Retrieve information about a specific ghost.
- `GET /attribution_trigger` — Retrieve attribution trigger data.

### Data Write (4)
- `POST /{id}/` — Write data to a specific endpoint identified by ID.
- `POST /5wwy/ga/g/c` — Write data to a specific data collection endpoint.
- `POST /api/v1/ghost/event` — Report an event to the ghost service.
- `POST /i/v0/e/` — Write data to a specific data collection endpoint.

### Config (1)
- `GET /v1/init` — Retrieve initial configuration data.

